extraction_notes: |
  - Dragons and Gods printed 42-44 (cache p043-p045, page_offset 1); the stat block starts on printed 42 (alignment through weight), printed 43 is a full-page illustration, and the block resumes at Natural A.R. on printed 44 and runs to the Rifts conversion there. Printed 42 and 44 were rendered and every number read off the render; the text layer''s digit cipher (LQ. for I.Q., 1 2 for 12) disagreed with it throughout.
  - PLAYER CHARACTER: printed 50, Hatchling Dragon as an optional Player Character, allows a hatchling of most species (not the Hydra, Cockatrice or Wooly Dragon), with the shared dragon experience table and no starting possessions (starting_money 0, equipment_starting empty). Imported 2026-09-27 on Nate''s decision, in the shape of chiang-ku-dragon: a hatchling and an adult variant, the hatchling first.
  - XP: the Dragon Exp. Table, printed 17, read off a render. The book prints 30 levels; the fifteen lower bounds stored are levels 1-15 (0 to 600,001). Levels 16-30 are recorded on serpent-of-the-wind-dragon.
  - POOLS AND DICE are per variant, as printed. A.R. is prose, as on the Chiang-Ku.
  - ATTACKS: attacks_base per variant, five for the hatchling and seven for the adult; no Hand to Hand style is printed or granted.
  - SAVES: "+2 on all other saving throws" (hatchling; +4 adult) is stored on each of the sheet''s d20 saves other than horror factor, which is stated separately. Coma/death is a percentile roll and is left alone.
  - MAGIC AND PSIONICS are the HATCHLING''s, because a variant cannot override either block and the hatchling is the player character. The adult''s are the two special abilities above. All wizard spells of levels one and two are granted by name: every catalog spell of levels 1-2 with no tradition whose system is NULL, palladium-fantasy or both (28 on 2026-09-27). Rows added later will not be granted. The 1D4 more from levels 3-4 at even levels is dice-valued, which a spells_schedule count cannot hold, so it is prose in the Magic Knowledge ability (the cats-eye hatchling precedent, and the convention of the other hatchlings imported the same day).
  - PSIONICS: six from sensitive and physical, two more at levels 3, 7 and 12.
  - SKILLS: the R.C.C. list at the adult''s percentages, as printed. The hatchling rule (languages and basic math at 98%, advanced math and everything else at first-level proficiency) is one override on the hatchling, advanced math at the catalog 45. Literacy in four other languages plus six more spoken is ten Language: Other picks and four Literacy: Other picks (judgement, as on the other hatchlings of this batch). The picks are written as bonuses on the catalog rows (Language: Other 50 +48, Literacy: Other 30 +68, 98% at first level), because regression refuses a language pick frozen with a base. The 15 picks carry the +10% the book''s average-level line gives selected skills (judgement: the sentence sits under the adult NPC''s level, and it is read as the class''s skill bonus). Scholar/Technical is the catalog''s Technical.
  - The Rifts conversion (M.D.C. 1D6x1000+500 adult, 1D4x100+50 hatchling; a Rifts skill list) is a different system''s stats and is not stored.
  - Alignment (any, typically scrupulous 20%, unprincipled 25% or selfish 20%), size, weight, habitat, life span, enemies and allies are in the body.
