## Lore

Thunder lizards are large, wingless, emerald green and gold reptilian dragons that once dominated the Old Kingdom of the Palladium World. Today they are multi-dimensional adventurers and avid practitioners of magic. Most are of good alignment and protect the innocent and downtrodden; several are known to ride with knights and palladins of the Timiro and Bizantium Kingdoms. To see one is said to be a sign of good luck, and to befriend one honestly is to have a friend for life.

They adore Elves, like humans, and respect all creatures who strive to be the best they can be, valuing truthfulness, compassion, honor, nobility and mercy. They are the most human-like of dragons in emotion and behavior, and the most down to earth and friendly toward ordinary mortals. They look down on evil and manipulative dragons, who in turn consider them meddlers.

**Alignment:** Any, but typically scrupulous (20%), unprincipled (25%) or selfish (20%).

**Size:** 20 feet tall (6 m), up to 45 feet (13.7 m) long.

**Weight:** 20 tons.

**Habitat:** Can be found anywhere, but likes to be around Elves, humans and civilization; currently most common to the Old Kingdom and Eastern Territory.

**Average Life Span:** 6000 years, but some have been known to live to 9000.

**Enemies:** The forces of evil. They are loathed by Basilisks, Night Stalkers and Serpents of the Wind; Hydras like the challenge of fighting them.

**Allies:** Elves, Titans, Rahu-Men and all Champions of Light.

## GM Notes

The average equivalent experience level of an adult is 1D6+7. A hatchling player character is the G.M.''s option (printed 50): powerful by human standards but roughly comparable to a third or fourth level sorcerer or man at arms, and in temperament a child - brash, rash, emotional and curious. Hatchlings are extremely rare, and more than one in a party is unlikely.
